			<attacks>
				<description><![CDATA[]]></description>
				<attack identifier="50f07a76-932d-444b-b5d5-46042c6e07a6" name="Dagger" range="20/60" attack="+5 vs AC" damage="1d4+2 piercing" displayed="true" ability="Dexterity">
					<description><![CDATA[Finesse, Light, Thrown]]></description>
				</attack>
				<attack identifier="1337404f-a91e-4307-95cb-53f5c9a74519" name="Handaxe" range="20/60" attack="+4 vs AC" damage="1d6+1 slashing" displayed="true" ability="Strength">
					<description><![CDATA[Light, Thrown]]></description>
				</attack>
			</attacks>
			<backstory><![CDATA[Living his life as an adventurer, Arnyld was destined to do great things, he started adventuring after his human village was raided by Elves and Oogers, forcing him away from his family, he travelled for many years searching, only for the Primordial War to rip them apart. Permanently. Arnyld vowed to end this war, with little to no regard for his own life, while also fighting for others. Arnyld had come to the source of the chaos and was able to, on both the Primordial and Material planes, restore balance, but not without cost. In his last moments, his strength, resolve, and selflessness attracted the attention of Eldath, The Quiet One and she, in his last moments, offered him another chance at another, more peaceful life. In his last moments, Arnyld saved the continent from destruction. going on to live a peaceful and fulfilling life as his soul, in his last moments was transfered to a Nimblewright he had constructed to help him on his shipyard, many years ago. Kyp now remembers his heroic moments and remembers fondly, only a little foggy at times. At peace, now that those times are over. But something fells off, Kyp knows that Arnyld's days as a legend and a hero are over, the question as to whether or not Kyp's are, is so far an unanswered question.]]></backstory>
			<background-trinket>A gold coin minted in a fallen civilization</background-trinket>
			<background-traits>I often correct others when their lack of manners offends me.
Nothing pleases me more than a good meal, good company, and job well done.</background-traits>
			<background-ideals>Greater Good. I would gladly give my life to defend those who can’t defend themselves. (Good)</background-ideals>
			<background-bonds>A famous song is actually about one of my greatest battles.</background-bonds>
			<background-flaws>I really don’t know when to shut up.</background-flaws>
			<background>
				<feature name="Traveler">
					<description><![CDATA[You come from somewhere else, a place others couldn’t begin to understand. Perhaps your home is a unique corner of the Land of the Mists or another world entirely. In any case, you and other travelers have shared experiences. You can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate among sympathetic trading caravans, itinerant families, or displaced groups, so long as you don’t present yourself as a danger. Such groups will hide you from the law or anyone searching for you, though they won’t risk their lives for you. Additionally, you can tell whether an object you can see and touch is from your homeland with near perfect accuracy.]]></description>
				</feature>
			</background>
